{
  "id": "05350_akubisuru",
  "headword": "{欠伸|あくび}する",
  "reading": "あくびする",
  "part_of_speech": "suru verb",
  "gloss": "to yawn",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to yawn",
      "explanation": "To involuntarily open the mouth wide and breathe in deeply, usually when tired or bored."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "05350_akubisuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{眠|ねむ}くて{欠伸|あくび}が{出|で}る。",
      "english": "I'm so sleepy I keep yawning.",
      "notes": "欠伸が出る = to yawn (lit. yawns come out)",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "05350_akubisuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{会議中|かいぎちゅう}に{欠伸|あくび}をしないで。",
      "english": "Don't yawn during the meeting.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "05350_akubisuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{欠伸|あくび}は{伝染|でんせん}するらしい。",
      "english": "Yawning is apparently contagious.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "05350_akubisuru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{退屈|たいくつ}な{授業|じゅぎょう}で{何度|なんど}も{欠伸|あくび}をしてしまった。",
      "english": "I yawned many times during the boring class.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "05350_akubisuru_ex5",
      "japanese": "{隣|となり}の{人|ひと}が{大|おお}きな{欠伸|あくび}をしたら、{自分|じぶん}も{欠伸|あくび}が{出|で}てしまった。",
      "english": "When the person next to me let out a big yawn, I ended up yawning too.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The noun {欠伸|あくび} can be used with する to form a verb. The expression {欠伸|あくび}が{出|で}る is equally common.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {欠伸|あくび}をする: to yawn\n- {欠伸|あくび}が{出|で}る: to yawn (lit. a yawn comes out)\n- {大|おお}きな{欠伸|あくび}: a big yawn\n\nKANJI NOTE:\n{欠伸|あくび} literally means \"lacking stretch\" ({欠|けつ} = lack + {伸|しん} = stretch). Often written in hiragana.",
